  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>has infinitely many solutions, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>β</mi></math> is equal to</p>",
    "image": null
